<tr><th class="News">11-26</th><td class="News"><a title="Linkat is an Ubuntu-based Linux distribution developed by the Department of Education of the Government of Catalonia in Spain. It is intended as a free resource for the educational institutions as well as the wider community in the Catalan-speaking regions. The distribution features the Cinnamon desktop and provides a range of applications for educational, office, internet and multimedia tasks, all backed by professional technical support." href="linkat">Linkat</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">11-24</th><td class="News"><a title="Veldmuis Linux is a minimalist, Arch-based Linux distribution and live image with a branded KDE Plasma desktop. It features a custom set of &quot;Veldmuis&quot; packages, as well as signed Pacman repositories, keyring packaging, Calamares system installer, and systemd-boot installation. The distribution strives to stay intentionally small and limited in features, although additional software groups, such as those for gaming, development or NVIDIA support, are available for installation as optional sets." href="veldmuis">Veldmuis Linux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">11-23</th><td class="News"><a title="VolnOS is a beginner-friendly, Ubuntu-based desktop Linux distribution with built-in artificial intelligence features and the ability to run Windows applications. It features the Cinnamon desktop environment and a custom graphical system installer. The distribution includes the Wine compatibility layer, pre-configured at system level, that can execute .exe and .msi programs with a double click. It also uses an A/B partition scheme for backups and automatic rollbacks in case of a failed or interrupted update. VolnOS is designed for users who wish to switch to Linux, but still need to use certain Windows-only applications." href="volnos">VolnOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">11-22</th><td class="News"><a title="Sloth OS is a beginner-friendly desktop and gaming Linux distribution based on Kinoite, one of Fedora's immutable variants, featuring a customised KDE Plasma desktop. It offers a number of desktop layouts, resembling those employed by other popular operating systems. The distribution also comes with a custom graphical system installer, a comprehensive configuration tool called &quot;Sloth Center&quot;, and support for running some Windows applications via the Wine compatibility layer. Gamers are catered for, with pre-configured Steam platform, TV mode, controllers and graphics drivers. Sloth OS also offers automatic updates with system rollback options." href="sloth">Sloth OS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">11-21</th><td class="News"><a title="kumaOS is a minimalist and immutable Fedora-based Linux distribution featuring the niri Wayland compositor and a custom-built shell called &quot;kumaUI&quot;. The shell provides a complete desktop user interface with a top bar, an application launcher, drawer panels, a lock screen, a file manager, a terminal and a system monitor. Like most immutable distributions, kumaOS also include atomic updates and rollbacks to a previous state." href="kumaos">kumaOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">11-20</th><td class="News"><a title="matrixOS is a Gentoo-based, immutable and gaming-friendly Linux distribution for desktops and servers. It is distributed in two file formats - IMG for flashing external storage devices, and QCOW2 for use in virtual machines. The desktop variants offer a choice of COSMIC and GNOME desktops, both in their vanilla forms. Additional software can be installed using flatpak or snap packages. While the project's primary goal is to provide a stable system with atomic upgrades and rollback options, the distribution also aims to be gaming-friendly, with NVIDIA and AMD GPUs optimisations and inclusion of Steam and Lutris gaming platforms." href="matrixos">matrixOS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">11-19</th><td class="News"><a title="Devario OS is an independent Linux distribution with Arch Linux package ecosystem compatibility. Its principal components include Aqueous tiling Wayland compositor, Pearl desktop shell and Shelly package manager. The project maintains its own system integration, signed package repositories, Linux kernel, desktop defaults, installer and release validation. The live and installed systems use Devario repositories by default; Arch repositories are not included in the default configuration. Devario OS is built by Seafoam Labs and is intended for general desktop use." href="devario">Devario OS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">11-18</th><td class="News"><a title="Caelaris Linux is a performance-optimised, rolling-release distribution based on Arch Linux. It ships three popular desktops - GNOME, Hyprland (with dynamic window tiling) and KDE Plasma, with a tool that enables rapid, on-the-fly switching between the three of them. The distribution provides a custom graphical system installer and offers a range of optimisations designed to improve high-performance gaming and low-latency tuning. It also includes several native applications, such as Caelaris Store (a software centre), Caelaris Defender (a security daemon that scans downloaded files for various types of malware), Caelaris About &amp; Settings (a system dashboard) and Caelaris Welcome (a utility providing quick access to essential configuration, gaming drivers, desktop tour and documentation." href="caelaris">Caelaris Linux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">11-15</th><td class="News"><a title="Simple OS is a minimalist, Debian-based desktop Linux distribution featuring a customised Openbox window manager. The project's goal is to build a Linux operating system that does not require the use of a terminal for common tasks, including software and system updates. Simple OS can be tested in live mode and installed to a hard disk using the Calamares system installer." href="simpleos">Simple OS</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">11-11</th><td class="News"><a title="Arctic Linux is a Fedora-based desktop Linux distribution featuring the keyboard-friendly Mango tiling window manager. It uses the Quickshell desktop shell. The distribution can be tested in live mode, but it can also be installed to a hard disk using a custom graphical system installation wizard - either from the initial boot menu or by launching the Arctic installer while in live mode. The installer, which employs disk encryption on a Btrfs filesystem, can download and install additional software. Arctic Linux provides its own repository of custom applications, while also supporting installation of flatpak packages and integration of Nix packages from NixOS." href="arctic">Arctic Linux</a></td></tr>
<tr><th class="News">11-10</th><td class="News"><a title="VoidStation is a media center Linux distribution based on Void. It features the Openbox window manager customised to present available applications as large tiles, so that they can be viewed easily and launched from a distance by a remote device, such as gamepads, remote controls, mice, keyboard, game console controllers, USB pads and joysticks. The user interface is configured to open an on-screen keyboard for every input field. Additional applications, games, gaming platforms and streaming services can be added using the included AppCenter. VoidStation also comes with pre-configured themes, adjustable scaling and resolution options, and support for all major European languages." href="voidstation">VoidStation</a></td></tr>
