        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The <a href="clonezilla">Clonezilla</a> Live Linux distribution has a new release which introduces experimental support for working with ZFS pools. "<span class="Quote">Stable Clonezilla Live 3.3.5-3 released. This release of Clonezilla Live includes major enhancements and bug fixes. Enhancements and changes since 3.3.3-37: the underlying GNU/Linux operating system has been upgraded, this release is based on the Debian 'Sid' repository as of 2026-11-15; the Linux kernel has been updated to 7.3.6; Partclone has been updated to version 0.3.54, which supports ZFS; added ZFS filesystem support for saving, restoring and cloning; implemented shadow VG LVM cloning using Partclone so that disk-to-disk cloning for LVM can be more efficient; support Windows Load Options in EFI NVRAM to prevent duplicate boot entries; added support for zxc (-z10p) and kanzi (-z11p) compression formats (experimental, as both upstream formats are actively evolving); allow compression programs in dd mode without falling back to gzip. Added a dialog in the Clonezilla main menu to choose Clonezilla alias block device names based on the PCI bus order; the default image name now contains minutes; support Btrfs subvolumes for openSUSE Tumbleweed in ocs-update-initrd; allow partclone-static as an alternative dependency....</span>" Additional information is provided in the <a href="https://sourceforge.net/p/clonezilla/news/2026/11/stable-clonezilla-live-335-3-released/">release notes</a>. <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/clonezilla/files/clonezilla_live_stable/3.3.5-3/">Download (MD5)</a>: <a href="https://downloads.sourceforge.net/clonezilla/clonezilla-live-3.3.5-3-amd64.iso">clonezilla-live-3.3.5-3-amd64.iso</a> (499MB, <a href="table.php?distribution=clonezilla&amp;pkglist=true&amp;version=3.3.5-3#pkglist">pkglist</a>).</td>
