        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The <a href="proxmox">Proxmox</a> project has published a new release, Proxmox 9.3 "Virtual Environment" which introduces new administration tools and runs on version 7.0 of the Linux kernel. "<span class="Quote">We are excited to announce the release of Proxmox Virtual Environment 9.3. This release focuses on simplifying SAN and multipath setups across clusters, enabling reliable guest tracking across migrations and backups via unique guest identities, improving routine maintenance and troubleshooting in the web UI, and expanding Software-Defined Networking (SDN) and installer security capabilities. Proxmox VE 9.3 is based on Debian 13.8 'Trixie' and includes Linux kernel 7.0 as the stable default (with kernel 7.3 available as an opt-in). In addition to core system enhancements, this update integrates the latest versions of our key underlying technologies, including QEMU 11.1, LXC 7.0, and ZFS 2.4. Here are the highlights in Proxmox VE 9.3: Cluster-wide multipath and SAN view (iSCSI, Fibre Channel, NVMe-oF); snapshots as volume chains on thick-provisioned LVM; HA maintenance mode via GUI; GUI support for custom storage plugins; unique guest identities for VMs and containers; nested notification match rules; SDN: Dedicated VRFs for Simple zones, live WireGuard status; Ceph Tentacle 20.2 as stable default alongside Ceph Umbrella 21.2 as option.</span>" Additional information is provided through the <a href="https://forum.proxmox.com/threads/proxmox-virtual-environment-9-3-released.187800/">release announcement</a> and <a href="https://pve.proxmox.com/wiki/Roadmap">release notes</a>. <a href="https://www.proxmox.com/en/downloads">Download (SHA256)</a>: <a href="https://enterprise.proxmox.com/iso/proxmox-ve_9.3-1.iso">proxmox-ve_9.3-1.iso</a> (1,724MB, <a href="https://enterprise.proxmox.com/iso/proxmox-ve_9.3-1.iso.torrent">torrent</a>, <a href="table.php?distribution=proxmox&amp;pkglist=true&amp;version=9.3#pkglist