        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">About two years ago the <a href="peppermint">Peppermint</a> project began experimenting with a new branch, based on Void, which would be developed in parallel with the distribution's Debian and Devuan editions. The first stable release of Peppermint OS's Void branch (PepVoid) has been published: "<span class="Quote">We are excited to announce the release of Peppermint OS Void. As a true rolling release, our goal with this edition is to expand your choice of system bases past the Debian and Devuan families. If you have been around the Peppermint community for a while, you know we maintain a few different branches. Our Flagship editions are intentionally minimal, keeping pre-installed software light so you have a clean slate to build the system your way. On the other hand, our 'Loaded' branch comes with applications pre-installed out of the box. It has been a while since we released a Loaded edition, we felt it was the best starting point for Peppermint Void which is why you will notice the ISO is quite large at around 4GB. For those who prefer a slimmer starting point, we will be releasing a Flagship build of this edition down the road. Just like our Debian and Devuan editions, this release uses XLibre as the display server.</span>" Further details can be found in the <a href="https://peppermintos.com/2026/11/peppermint-os-void-loaded-release/">release announcement</a>. <a href="https://peppermintos.com/trixie-base-downloads/">Download</a>: <a href="https://downloads.sourceforge.net/peppermintos/pepvoid-x86_64-linux-xfce-xlibre-loaded.iso"> (4,956MB, <a href="https://downloads.sourceforge.net/peppermintos/pepvoid-x86_64-linux-xfce-xlibre-loaded.iso.sha512">SHA512</a>, <a href="https://downloads.sourceforge.net/peppermintos/pepvoid-x86_64-linux-xfce-xlibre-loaded.iso.asc">signature</a>, <a href="table.php?distribution=peppermint&amp;pkglist=true&amp;version=2026-void#pkglist">pkglist</a>).</td>
