</td>
        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The KaOS project, which develops a rolling-release Linux distribution with focus on integrating the Qt development platform and KDE applications into a complete desktop, has announced the release of <a href="kaos">KaOS</a> 2026.11 live ISO images. This new version incorporates the Noctalia shell's recent improvements and new plugins: "<span class="Quote">It is with great pleasure to present to you the November release of a new stable ISO image. The niri/Noctalia setup for KaOS post-Plasma is further improved. Noctalia 5 has added an impressive list of plugins, expanding the functionality of this shell considerably. Adding dex for xdg autostart functionality in niri has improved the correct permissions, so things like using screen-recording just work again. KaOS has created a new application (kss) to still be able to adjust the KConfig Modules with a GUI. KaOS uses dinit, turnstile, seatd for the system startup, seats and services. The use of parts of the systemd application is further reduced. Parts still in use are mainly for udev and tmpfiles. Elogind is in use, though not for system login, but purely for a functional polkit. Openrc-settingsd is added to re-add standalone components for localed, timedated and timesyncd. The use of console-setup has been expanded to now also offer a standalone localectl replacement. The default display manager is greetd-based Tuigreet. Greetd fully integrates with seatd so is a better fit for KaOS in the new setup.</span>" See the <a href="https://kaosx.us/news/2026/kaos11/">release announcement</a> for further details and screenshots. <a href="https://kaosx.us/download">Download (SHA256)</a>: <a href="https://downloads.sourceforge.net/kaosx/KaOS-2026.11-x86_64.iso">KaOS-2026.11-x86_64.iso</a> (4,217MB, <a href="table.php?distribution=kaos&pkglist=true&version=2026.11#pkglist">pkglist</a>).</td>
