        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The CachyOS team has announced the availability of the November 2026 ISO image of <a href="cachyos">CachyOS</a>, an Arch-based Linux distribution featuring custom Linux kernels optimised for performance and gaming. The project's latest version includes a new kernel variant designed to run certain games and a fully-revamped application installer: "<span class="Quote">CachyOS November 2026 release. This is our sixth release of the year. This release brings support for Easy Anti-Cheat Linux v2. EAC only lets games start when it can verify how the system was booted - Secure Boot with a kernel signed by a key that Epic trusts, a TPM 2.0, an enabled IOMMU, and a kernel running in lockdown mode that only loads signed modules. For this we provide a dedicated kernel, linux-cachyos-eac, together with a systemd-boot signed with the same key. The EAC kernel gets its own boot entry and your normal boot entries are kept, so you only boot into it when you want to play a game that uses EAC. ... The CachyOS Package Installer has been fully revamped with a new UI for its 2.0.0 release. Besides the CachyOS and Arch repositories, it can now build packages from the AUR and install Flatpak apps and AppImages, each of them opt-in. Before an AUR package gets built, the PKGBUILD and its install scripts are shown for review, and a static analysis marks the lines which should be looked at.</span>" Read the rest of the detailed <a href="https://cachyos.org/blog/2611-november-release/">release announcement</a> for more information. <a href="https://cachyos.org/download">Download</a>: <a href="https://cdn77.cachyos.org/ISO/desktop/261122/cachyos-desktop-linux-261122.iso">cachyos-desktop-linux-261122.iso</a> (3,081MB, <a href="https://cdn77.cachyos.org/ISO/desktop/261122/cachyos-desktop-linux-261122.iso.sha256">SHA256</a>, <a href="https://cdn77.cachyos.org/ISO/desktop/261122/cachyos-desktop-linux-261122.iso.sig">signature</a>, <a href="https:/