        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The AnduinOS team has announced the release of <a href="anduin">AnduinOS</a> 2.1.0, an updated version of the project's Ubuntu-based Linux distribution with a highly customised GNOME desktop. This release is based on Ubuntu 26.10 and includes GNOME 51: "<span class="Quote">AnduinOS 2.1.0 brings Ubuntu 26.10 'Stonking Stingray', GNOME 51 and Linux 7.3 to AMD64 and ARM64. It is the first release in the AnduinOS 2 series based on a non-LTS Ubuntu version. Alongside it, AnduinOS 2.0.6 delivers the same desktop, installation, and recovery improvements on Ubuntu 26.04 LTS and GNOME 50. The Fluent login screen has been adapted to GNOME 51's sign-in controls, and the bundled desktop extensions have been updated for the new session. Fresh installations use the GTK 4 version of Desktop Icons NG. Appearance lets you choose AnduinOS application icons or use each app’s default icon. The selection now persists after screen locking and desktop extension reloads. Package updates also preserve your login-screen wallpaper. You can enable a window layout menu that appears when you drag a window to the top of the screen. It is off by default.</span>" See the <a href="https://news.aiursoft.com/post/2026/11/18/anduin-os-2-1-0-arrives-with-ubuntu-26-10-and-gnome-51">release announcement</a> and the <a href="https://docs.anduinos.com/Release-Notes/2.1.0.html">release notes</a> for more details and screenshots. <a href="https://www.anduinos.com/#download-links">Download</a>: <a href="https://cf.anduinos.com/AnduinOS-2.1.0-amd64.iso">AnduinOS-2.1.0.iso</a> (2,362MB, <a href="https://cf.anduinos.com/AnduinOS-2.1.0-amd64.sha256">SHA256</a>, <a href="https://cf.anduinos.com/AnduinOS-2.1.0-amd64.torrent">torrent</a>, <a href="table.php?distribution=anduin&pkglist=true&version=2.1.0#pkglist">pkglist</a>). A new build of AnduinOS 2.0 series, based on the long-term-supported Ubuntu 26.04, is also <a href="https://www.anduinos.com/#download-links"